@startuml
' ============================================================================
' METADATA
'   author:       TheRobotDrafts Examples
' '   description:  A 3-state traffic-light controller that cycles on timer events.
'   usecase:      Teach states (rounded rect), initial/final pseudostates, transitions with event[guard]/action.
'   complexity:   simple
'   domain:       embedded
' ============================================================================
title Example State Machine - Simple Traffic Light

' An INITIAL PSEUDOSTATE (filled circle) is written as [*].
' Its outgoing arrow points to the first real state.
[*] --> Red : power_on

' STATES are rendered as ROUNDED RECTANGLES.
' Two spellings: an implicit name (the word is the id) or an explicit form:
'   state "Display Name" as id
state "Red" as Red
state "Green" as Green
state "Yellow" as Yellow

' A TRANSITION is an arrow with an optional LABEL of the form:
'   event[guard]/action
'   - event:   the trigger that fires the transition
'   - guard:   a boolean condition in brackets (optional)
'   - action:  behavior run during the transition, after a slash (optional)
' All three parts are optional, but the slash must follow a guard or event.
Red --> Green : timer_expired[phase_complete]/switch_to_green
Green --> Yellow : timer_expired[phase_complete]/switch_to_yellow
Yellow --> Red : timer_expired[phase_complete]/switch_to_red

' A FINAL PSEUDOSTATE (bullseye) ends the region. A traffic light normally
' never terminates, but here is how one would be reached:
Red --> [*] : power_off

' TEACHING NOTES:
'   - A state machine has exactly ONE initial pseudostate per region.
'   - The traffic light has no final state in normal operation — it loops.
'   - event[guard]/action: if the guard is false, the event does NOT fire,
'     and the object stays in the current state.
@enduml
